Bugfix: Make the chunked-upload transfer lock effective for all file names

The lock that serialises the size accounting of a chunked upload was keyed on the
raw chunk prefix, so its key grew with the file name. Both the database and the
memcache locking provider reject keys longer than 64 characters, which meant the
lock silently never engaged for longer file names - exactly the large uploads it
is meant to protect. The variable part of the key is now hashed, so the key has a
constant length.

In addition, a disabled file locking ("filelocking.enabled" => false) hands out a
locking provider that accepts every lock without locking anything. That was
treated as a successfully held lock, so the size subtotal was written
incrementally while nothing was serialised. Such installations now take the
documented fallback and recount the subtotal instead.
